        "original_id": "e9d8c111-de9f-5094-8ed8-0e924d1964f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Foxhound, English Foxhound, Löwchen, Little Lion Dog, Trigg Hound, Trigg Foxhound, Hayden Trigg Hound\n- People: Colonel Haiden Trigg\n- Places: Kentucky\n- Concepts: dog breeds, dog varieties, name translations\n\nFacts:\n- The American Foxhound is a breed of dog and a cousin of the English Foxhound.\n- The Löwchen, also called the Little Lion Dog, is a breed of dog.\n- The name Löwchen is German for “little lion,” and the French name Petit chien lion means “little lion dog.”\n- The Trigg Hound, also known as the Trigg Foxhound or Hayden Trigg Hound, is a variety of the American Foxhound.\n- Colonel Haiden Trigg developed the Trigg Hound in Kentucky.",
